{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowConcrete","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowConcrete","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_hecke_forces_trivial_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_hecke_forces_trivial_twist","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L148-L169","doc":"**Hecke capstone — the de-opaqued gate forces `θ^f = 1` on every block.**\n\nTake the concrete RT row `bwS0Concrete (heckeVerlindeData …) (theta q) f` on the Hecke Verlinde data.\nIf it equals the Hecke modular datum `d_q(λ)/√(Σ d_q²)` for **all** `λ ∈ P` (the de-opaqued form of\n`bwS0_eq_hecke`), then `∀ l ∈ P, (theta q l)^f = 1` — the forced Seifert framing must be twist-trivial.\n\nAt real `q₀ > 1` this is **false** off the self-conjugate blocks (`theta q₀ l = q₀^{c(λ)}` is not a\nroot of unity for `c(λ) ≠ 0`), so for the physical forced framing `f ≠ 0` the gate is **REFUTED** at\n`q₀` — the honest disposition.  The residue is the fibre root-of-unity form (`|q| = 1`), unaffected. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_S0_forces_trivial_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_S0_forces_trivial_twist","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L140-L146","doc":"**Abstract capstone.**  If the concrete row equals `S_{0λ}` and the row is nonzero, then the\nframing twist is trivial: `θ_λ^f = 1`.  (Immediate from `bwS0Concrete_eq_S0_iff` + `Or.resolve_left`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_breaks_symmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_breaks_symmetry","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L121-L136","doc":"**The concrete row breaks conjugation symmetry.**  If the transpose-twist power differs from the\ntwist power (`(θ_λ)⁻¹^f ≠ (θ_λ)^f` — the framing asymmetry) and the row is nonzero, then\n`bwS0Concrete(λ') ≠ bwS0Concrete(λ)`: the concrete RT vacuum row is **not** transpose-invariant, unlike\n`d_q`/`S0`.  Hence it cannot equal the transpose-symmetric `d_q/D` for `f ≠ 0`.\n\nAt real `q₀ > 1` with `θ_λ = q₀^{c(λ)}`: `(θ_λ)⁻¹^f = q₀^{-f·c(λ)}` and `(θ_λ)^f = q₀^{f·c(λ)}` are\nunequal whenever `f·c(λ) ≠ 0`, so the hypothesis holds off the self-conjugate blocks — the proved\nobstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_conj_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_conj_mul","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L105-L119","doc":"**Conjugation product law.**  Using `S_{0λ'} = S_{0λ}` (transpose-invariance of `d_q`) and\n`θ_{λ'} = θ_λ⁻¹` (transpose-inversion of the twist), the concrete row at `λ` and at the transpose `λ'`\nmultiply to `S_{0λ}²`:  `bwS0Concrete(λ')·bwS0Concrete(λ) = S_{0λ}²`.  The `θ^f` factors cancel — the\nrow's framing dependence is transpose-antisymmetric while `S0` is transpose-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_of_twist_pow_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_of_twist_pow_one","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L94-L98","doc":"**Trivial twist ⇒ the gate holds** (the clean direction, `θ^f = 1 → bwS0Concrete = S0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_S0_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_eq_S0_iff","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**The de-opaqued gate holds iff the twist power is trivial.**\n`bwS0Concrete = S_{0λ} ↔ (S_{0λ} = 0 ∨ θ_λ^f = 1)`.  Factoring `S_{0λ}·θ^f = S_{0λ}·1`, either the\nrow vanishes or the framing twist is trivial — the framing obstruction, exact and symbolic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_f_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_f_zero","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**The `f = 0` tautology (content-free).**  Zero Seifert framing carries no Σ(2,3,5) data: the\nconcrete row collapses to the compact modular datum `S_{0λ}`.  This is exactly the case the opaque\ngate cannot distinguish from a genuine framing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BWVacuumRowConcrete.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**The concrete RT/Seifert vacuum S-matrix row** — the compact modular datum `S_{0λ}` times the\nribbon twist `θ_λ` raised to the **forced Seifert framing** `f : ℤ`.  This is the genuine formula that\nreplaces the opaque, fiat-dischargeable free field `bwS0` in `BWVacuumRowIsHecke`: it is\n`S^{RT}_{0λ} = S_{0λ}·θ_λ^{f}`, the colored-WRT vacuum row of the framed Seifert manifold `S³/2I`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}